From 69a62b869ed4a176d8136223649ce979cb8f9388 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:21:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: start the spare lantern scan at the first lantern

With no flask of oil, the Borg looks for a spare lantern to refuel from.
The scan is meant to walk the lanterns from the first one, skipping
Everburning and empty ones, but it started at borg_slot(), which returns
the last lantern in the pack. If that one was empty or Everburning the
scan ended at once, so an earlier lantern with fuel was never used and
the wielded lantern ran dry. Start at the first lantern in the pack.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#90.

(cherry picked from commit bd4698a850e9fb926d74c9a26be298716a33e5ba)
---
 src/borg/borg-light.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-light.c b/src/borg/borg-light.c
index af9fdfc11..13f50db6d 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-light.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-light.c
@@ -559,7 +559,13 @@ static bool borg_refuel_lantern(void)
     /* None available check for lantern */
     if (i < 0) {
         /* get first lantern */
-        i = borg_slot(TV_LIGHT, sv_light_lantern);
+        for (i = 0; i < z_info->pack_size; i++) {
+            if (borg_items[i].iqty && borg_items[i].tval == TV_LIGHT
+                && borg_items[i].sval == sv_light_lantern)
+                break;
+        }
+        if (i >= z_info->pack_size)
+            i = -1;
 
         if (i >= 0) {
             /* loop through lanterns (they should be next to each other) */
